intuition: GA_Rel*/GA_RelSpecial flags, BOOPSI GadgetInfo and redraws as on 3.1 (BGUI)

Reference probes tests/probes/intuition/gadinfo and openrefresh:
- GA_RelWidth/RelHeight/RelSpecial set GFLG_RELWIDTH/RELHEIGHT/RELSPECIAL;
- gi_Domain is the whole window (inner box for GZZ) for every method,
  also SetGadgetAttrsA and DoGadgetMethodA;
- GM_LAYOUT (gpl_Initial 0) after every window resize;
- a gadget list is rendered back to front;
- SetWindowTitles() redraws no application gadget, window (de)activation
  only border gadgets;
- SetGadgetAttrsA() renders nothing itself (only on behalf of lxa's
  built-in classes, which do not render in OM_SET yet);
- a new window gets no IDCMP_REFRESHWINDOW and no LAYERREFRESH;
- BeginUpdate() with no damage clips all rendering.
With GFLG_REL* set, lxa's SetWindowTitles() redrew BGUI's master group,
which clears its area while Typeface's character gadget only draws once:
that was why setting the flags blanked Typeface's character buttons.
devpac_scrollbar_gtest: the stipple expectation contradicted the
reference (the container is pen 3 throughout); asserts that now.

