powermonger: 139th pass -- the game's own text names the fields: group states, lord ranks, posture, aggression, age; the animals are sheep; the captain panel's loyalty line is a constant

The UI text tables in $9000..$b000 are read through small selector routines, so their strings are the developers' words for the bytes the selectors index:
- group state 1..16: Waiting, Get Food, Get Men, Meeting, Going To, In Camp, Go Home, Attack, Invent, Equip, Pickup, Supply, Fighting, Alliance, Trading, Spying (3, 6, 8, 13 seen);
- lord kind 1..6: Village, Hamlet, Town, City, Capital, Base (the 17-building Capital round a Tower; Base is mission 1's single Tower);
- posture 2/3/4 Aggressive/Neutral/Passive, aggression 0..7 PowerMonger..Wimp (136/148 of the group array, the table's "AI sub-state scratch" corrected), speed words, age classes (byte 14 is age in years, men start at 12..43), side names, the person, house, mine, tree and animal panels;
- category 8 reads "Sheep", the category $22 the animal loop also takes reads "Cow" and nothing creates it;
- the loyalty selector $9116 is move.w #3,D0: the panel always says "trusting" (callcap on two snapshots: A5 = $95c1).

Add flyers to the game: masked blitter objects, with a temporary demo driving them

flyers.s erases and draws 16x16 masked objects into the back screen;
gfx.s holds the graphics built from the user's ROM by tools/make_gfx.py;
demo.s stands in for the game and bounces ten flyers around. Ten flyers
take about 60 raster lines.

